- the index exists in /data/abc.txt 
How is memory stored?
1. We store it in 2 points: 
  a. INNODE - metadata- Owner, Group, Permission, SIZE, Time, Creation or Last modified df -hTi 
  b. DATA
- Even if the file gets deleted, the inode helps us with the recovery 
- as the os interacts with the inode, if the inode is full, the memory is full even though we have some memory 
-hT - human-readable 
df -T - shows me the type of files
df -hT - shows me in human-readable with the type 
note: in memory, IT need not be a consecutive 

