LINKS:-
- In the windows, I can create a shortcut 
- so that short cut are called links 
- If we delete the links, it doesn't remove the data but just that shortcut
- is it possible to create links for directories?
  - we cannot create it for directories 
- Will it be created in the same directory?
  - it need not be created in the same directory

  - Hard Link:
        - It is the same but called different, but it refers to the same thing (kind of creating a copy but we are not duplicating the memory but we are referencing it through the same inode)
        - the use of the Hardlink is the need for the backup 
    
  - Soft Link:
        - Shortcut (it references to that original file )

- ln - create links (ln <target> <directory>)
- so we have created a file and now create a hard link in the hard link if we made the modifications, that will get reflected in the original file 
- ln -s <target> <directory> - this will create a soft link  - when we create a soft link file and update it, the soft link will also get updated 
ls -li gives info of inodes 
- the parameters of the hard link and original files are the same.
- but the soft link has a different
- the soft link looks like abc-soft-link.txt -> abc.txt


